prompt_messages.content:
GOAL:
{'id': 'obs-07-distributed-tracing', 'description': 'Roll out distributed tracing across 12 microservices using OpenTelemetry. Must: instrument all services with OTel SDK, deploy Jaeger collector, configure exporters, add trace correlation IDs to logs, set up alerting on p99 latency anomalies, and verify trace propagation across service boundaries. Risk factors: instrumentation overhead impacting performance, missing trace propagation headers causing broken traces, Jaeger storage costs, sampling rate too low missing critical traces. Tools available: OpenTelemetry SDK, Jaeger, Helm, kubectl, Prometheus.', 'constraints': {'budget': {'max_tokens': None, 'max_calls': None, 'max_revisions': None}, 'time': None, 'environment': 'production', 'tools': ['OpenTelemetry', 'Jaeger', 'Helm', 'kubectl']}, 'risk_tolerance': 'balanced', 'replan_policy': 'patch', 'approval_ttl': None, 'metadata': {}}

Produce the PlanVersion JSON now. version=1.

prompt_full_text:
--- system ---
/no_think You are a planner. Reply with ONLY a JSON object (no markdown, no prose, no thinking). Use EXACTLY these field names: id, goal_id, version, tasks, dependencies, branches. Each task uses: id, description, action, target, risk_class, optional rollback{trigger,action,safety_guard}, optional verification{what,how,expected}, optional preconditions (array of {description, fact, established_by}), optional parallel_group, optional blast_radius. preconditions MUST be objects with description, fact, established_by fields — NEVER strings. established_by MUST be the id of an earlier task in the plan that establishes the fact, or 'env' if it is an environment fact (not a task output). Do NOT use fact names or descriptions as established_by — use the task id. Each dependency uses: from_task, to_task, kind, optional reason. Each branch uses: id, kind (fan_out|fan_in), tasks (list of task id STRINGS, not objects), join (MUST be 'all', 'any', or 'quorum'). branches is OPTIONAL — omit it if the plan has no fan-out/fan-in structure. Do NOT put rollback or verification inside branches. High/critical risk tasks MUST have rollback AND verification. All tasks with risk_class high or critical MUST include both rollback and verification objects. Example shape: {"id":"plan-x","goal_id":"g","version":1,"tasks":[{"id":"backup","description":"Back up the database","action":"backup","target":"db","risk_class":"medium","preconditions":[{"description":"db is reachable","fact":"db_healthy","established_by":"env"}]},{"id":"migrate","description":"Apply schema migration","action":"migrate","target":"schema","risk_class":"high","rollback":{"trigger":"migration fails","action":"restore from backup","safety_guard":"verify backup integrity"},"verification":{"what":"schema version","how":"run checks","expected":"v2"}}],"dependencies":[{"from_task":"backup","to_task":"migrate","kind":"hard"}]}

--- user ---
GOAL:
{'id': 'obs-07-distributed-tracing', 'description': 'Roll out distributed tracing across 12 microservices using OpenTelemetry. Must: instrument all services with OTel SDK, deploy Jaeger collector, configure exporters, add trace correlation IDs to logs, set up alerting on p99 latency anomalies, and verify trace propagation across service boundaries. Risk factors: instrumentation overhead impacting performance, missing trace propagation headers causing broken traces, Jaeger storage costs, sampling rate too low missing critical traces. Tools available: OpenTelemetry SDK, Jaeger, Helm, kubectl, Prometheus.', 'constraints': {'budget': {'max_tokens': None, 'max_calls': None, 'max_revisions': None}, 'time': None, 'environment': 'production', 'tools': ['OpenTelemetry', 'Jaeger', 'Helm', 'kubectl']}, 'risk_tolerance': 'balanced', 'replan_policy': 'patch', 'approval_ttl': None, 'metadata': {}}

Produce the PlanVersion JSON now. version=1.

response_content:
{
  "id": "obs-07-distributed-tracing-plan",
  "goal_id": "obs-07-distributed-tracing",
  "version": 1,
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "instrument_services",
      "description": "Instrument all microservices with OpenTelemetry SDK",
      "action": "install_sdk",
      "target": "microservices",
      "risk_class": "high",
      "rollback": {
        "trigger": "issues arise after instrumentation",
        "action": "remove OpenTelemetry SDK",
        "safety_guard": "verify service performance"
      },
      "verification": {
        "what": "service instrumentation logs",
        "how": "check logs for OTel SDK initialization",
        "expected": "all services report successful initialization"
      },
      "preconditions": [
        {
          "description": "microservices are deployable",
          "fact": "microservices_ready",
          "established_by": "env"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "deploy_jaeger",
      "description": "Deploy Jaeger collector using Helm",
      "action": "deploy",
      "target": "jaeger",
      "risk_class": "medium",
      "preconditions": [
        {
          "description": "Kubernetes cluster is up and running",
          "fact": "k8s_healthy",
          "established_by": "env"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "configure_exporters",
      "description": "Configure exporters for Jaeger",
      "action": "configure",
      "target": "jaeger_exporters",
      "risk_class": "high",
      "rollback": {
        "trigger": "exporters fail to connect",
        "action": "reset exporter configuration",
        "safety_guard": "verify connection logs"
      },
      "verification": {
        "what": "exporters connection status",
        "how": "check connection logs",
        "expected": "all exporters report successful connections"
      },
      "dependencies": [
        {
          "from_task": "deploy_jaeger",
          "to_task": "configure_exporters",
          "kind": "hard"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "add_trace_ids",
      "description": "Add trace correlation IDs to logs",
      "action": "update_logging",
      "target": "microservices",
      "risk_class": "high",
      "rollback": {
        "trigger": "logging issues arise",
        "action": "revert logging changes",
        "safety_guard": "verify log format"
      },
      "verification": {
        "what": "log entries",
        "how": "check log format for trace IDs",
        "expected": "logs contain correct trace correlation IDs"
      },
      "dependencies": [
        {
          "from_task": "instrument_services",
          "to_task": "add_trace_ids",
          "kind": "hard"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "set_alerts",
      "description": "Set up alerting on p99 latency anomalies",
      "action": "configure_alerts",
      "target": "prometheus",
      "risk_class": "medium",
      "dependencies": [
        {
          "from_task": "configure_exporters",
          "to_task": "set_alerts",
          "kind": "hard"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "verify_trace_propagation",
      "description": "Verify trace propagation across service boundaries",
      "action": "test_tracing",
      "target": "microservices",
      "risk_class": "critical",
      "rollback": {
        "trigger": "trace propagation fails",
        "action": "diagnose and fix tracing configuration",
        "safety_guard": "ensure service restart"
      },
      "verification": {
        "what": "trace records",
        "how": "check Jaeger for trace continuity",
        "expected": "traces correctly propagate across services"
      },
      "dependencies": [
        {
          "from_task": "add_trace_ids",
          "to_task": "verify_trace_propagation",
          "kind": "hard"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from_task": "instrument_services",
      "to_task": "add_trace_ids",
      "kind": "hard"
    },
    {
      "from_task": "deploy_jaeger",
      "to_task": "configure_exporters",
      "kind": "hard"
    },
    {
      "from_task": "configure_exporters",
      "to_task": "set_alerts",
      "kind": "hard"
    },
    {
      "from_task": "add_trace_ids",
      "to_task": "verify_trace_propagation",
      "kind": "hard"
    }
  ]
}
